{"ruling": "refund_partial", "amount": 4.17, "recommended_action": "Issue a $4.17 Ryde voucher to the rider (NS-7 form) for the unexempted 2.96 km off-route segment; record the RD-1 shortest-direct-route breach on the driver's file but attach no account flag.", "confidence": 0.9, "reasoning": "This is a completed RydeTAXI trip billed on a metered breakdown (base $3.90, distance $34.84, time $12.96, platform $1.47, total $53.17), with no waiting charge and a 1.0× surge [F6][F5]. The fare model makes distance-driven metered trips the category where detour kilometres flow into the fare, so the metered branch of the remedy applies [F6][RD-2]. The GPS record shows one off-route segment, 09:32–09:38, in which 2.96 km were driven where the optimal route covers 0.00 km, reaching up to 974 m from it [F3]; that is an unexplained deviation from the shortest and most direct route and engages the driver's routing duty [F3][RD-1].

